<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::maritime_harassment_rate" target="global_financial_stress::cross_border_capital_flo" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">More frequent maritime harassment raises insurance and trade‑finance costs and prompts exporters, importers and portfolio investors to delay, reroute or withdraw exposures to the corridor and nearby markets, reducing net cross‑border capital flows to and through those jurisdictions.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::maritime_harassment_rate" target="middle_east_escalation::maritime_transit_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Increased harassment of merchant shipping in theaters tied to the Russia–Ukraine war prompts commercial rerouting and concentration of traffic through Middle East chokepoints (e.g., Suez, Strait of Hormuz), raising the probability and expected severity of disruptive incidents there.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::maritime_harassment_rate" target="security_alliance_shift::critical_materials" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Increased harassment of commercial shipping raises transit losses, insurance and diversion costs on routes that carry critical commodities, directly lowering predictable access to those materials for importing firms.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">security_alliance_shift</data>
</edge>
