<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" target="global_financial_stress::bond_market_liquidity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Stronger coalition cohesion enables coordinated financial measures (sanctions, de‑risking guidance and correspondent‑bank restrictions) that remove market‑makers and clearing access for targeted issuers, causing an immediate drying up of bond market liquidity in affected markets and spillovers to related instruments.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" target="middle_east_escalation::sanctions_enforcement" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Stronger policy alignment among external allies responding to the Russia–Ukraine war produces coordinated diplomatic pressure, intelligence-sharing and secondary measures that increase the intensity and reach of sanctions enforcement affecting energy transactions tied to Middle East actors.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" target="middle_east_escalation::conflict_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher cohesion among Western and external security partners reduces perceived windows of opportunity for regional proxies and states in the Middle East by strengthening deterrence and coordinated support to threatened partners, lowering the rate and scale of kinetic escalation.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" target="security_alliance_shift::industrial_subsidy_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Greater policy alignment among external partners produces coordinated decisions to finance domestic defence and dual‑use industrial capacity, increasing the scale of targeted subsidies and assistance to affected sectors.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">security_alliance_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" target="security_alliance_shift::tariff_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter cohesion enables allied governments to impose synchronized trade measures (tariffs/embargoes) on identified suppliers linked to the conflict, raising effective tariff intensity in targeted trade lines.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">security_alliance_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::regulatory_restrictions" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.9</data>
  <data key="d36">Stronger cohesion among the US and allied states after Russia's aggression produces coordinated policy responses—joint export controls, sanction packages and tighter licensing—directly increasing the stringency and enforcement of restrictions on technology and infrastructure transfers affecting China.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::ai_capex_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Improved allied policy alignment triggers coordinated public R&amp;D funding, procurement commitments and risk-sharing measures that raise firms' and governments' willingness to commit larger AI infrastructure and cloud capex within allied ecosystems to sustain a technological lead over China.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
