<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::ai_capex_rate" target="global_financial_stress::cross_border_capital_flo" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">An acceleration in AI capital spending by major firms drives outbound FDI and cross-border project financing (cloud regions, hyperscale campuses, equipment purchases), producing measurable increases in net cross-border capital flows as funds are deployed abroad.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::ai_capex_rate" target="middle_east_escalation::conflict_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Faster AI capex by the US and China accelerates deployment of ISR, targeting and autonomous mission-planning tools to their regional partners and proxies in the Middle East, lowering operational risk and thresholds for conducting more frequent precision strikes and kinetic raids.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::ai_capex_rate" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_strike_intensit" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher AI capital spending accelerates commercial development of imagery‑analysis, targeting and battle‑management software that allied providers and contractors supply to Ukraine, improving targeting speed and enabling more frequent precision strikes.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::ai_capex_rate" target="security_alliance_shift::industrial_subsidy_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A rapid rise in corporate AI capital commitments raises political and economic incentives for governments to introduce or expand targeted subsidies and incentives to retain AI investment, talent and related supply chains domestically.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">security_alliance_shift</data>
</edge>
